{"id":215711460818415,"type":"album","name":"Moondance","artist":"Van Morrison","year":1970,"weight":25,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710604.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-1a1ce8e2-8742-4146-8f3f-172376f94468/mbid-1a1ce8e2-8742-4146-8f3f-172376f94468-10696308872.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":10,"country":"US","scaruffi":8.5,"aoty":94,"aoty_user":82,"yt":"UCDdpShvV_U","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/5PfnCqRbdfIDMb1x3MPQam","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_m_HGfcGMDBGX4u6z735fPNTC48-rMbeRA","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/van-morrison/moondance","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/6829-van-morrison-moondance.php"},"desc":"Moondance is the third solo album by Northern Irish singer-songwriter Van Morrison. It was released on Warner Bros. Records on 28 February 1970 and peaked at #29 on Billboard's Pop Albums chart. The album's musical style blends R&B;, folk rock, country rock, and also jazz (most obviously on the title track). The single released was \"Come Running\" with \"Crazy Love\" as the B-side, which peaked at #39 on the Pop Singles chart. \"Crazy Love\" was only released as a single in the Netherlands and did not chart. \"Moondance\", as a single was not released until 1977 and peaked at #92. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":163671524152735,"name":"Van Morrison","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Van-Morrison.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":265524373450282,"type":"genre","name":"jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1461,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":44294165522841,"type":"genre","name":"r&b","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":908,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":621,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":186201380116213,"type":"genre","name":"classic rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":268,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":87379772038769,"type":"genre","name":